{"id": "EUVD-2026-59479", "enisaUuid": "df0a942c-6a8c-37b3-95a0-500515bb5ed9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: amd: acp-sdw-sof: Bound DAI link iteration\n\ncreate_sdw_dailinks() walks sof_dais until it finds an entry with\ninitialised cleared, but sof_dais is allocated with exactly num_ends\nentries. If all entries are initialised, the loop reads past the end of\nthe array.\n\nPass the allocated entry count to create_sdw_dailinks() and stop before\nreading past the array.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:33", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a5ff4000dd7a390139dd7823fef1de4963e490a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e82497138abea7d5c6e65015663d907fbcbf6b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/86a64c049873fe4d4a6a378e27a333ab5631c4b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d992e63f52d58f52b724606c60ae7b37a1c582f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vwrj-mgjx-j4g8", "CVE-2026-74332"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04e93425-4ae3-383e-8315-c9436b99c38c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2054948a-544a-3a87-819c-1c229023e97e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d8348ddc56ed43ba39d1e8adda13299201f32ed <0a5ff4000dd7a390139dd7823fef1de4963e490a"}, {"id": "3a9216ad-c8c6-3f1d-b22f-be2ea1bfbefb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "59b002b5-54b3-3026-8927-3613b72e3ddb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d8348ddc56ed43ba39d1e8adda13299201f32ed <4d992e63f52d58f52b724606c60ae7b37a1c582f"}, {"id": "7d04fd07-5400-3523-a11f-adcf74cc4456", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2